      "ayah_id": "5:35",
      "ayah_arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ ٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَٱبۡتَغُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهِ ٱلۡوَسِيلَةَ وَجَٰهِدُواْ فِي سَبِيلِهِۦ لَعَلَّكُمۡ تُفۡلِحُونَ",
      "surah_revelation": "Medinan",
      "surah_name": "Al-Maaida",
      "literal_gloss": "the means",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "O you who have believed, fear Allah and seek the means [of nearness] to Him and strive in His cause that you may succeed.",
        "pickthall": "O ye who believe! Be mindful of your duty to Allah, and seek the way of approach unto Him, and strive in His way in order that ye may succeed.",
        "khattab": "O believers! Be mindful of Allah and seek what brings you closer to Him and struggle in His Way, so you may be successful",
        "arberry": "O believers, fear God, and seek the means to come to Him, and struggle in His way; haply you will prosper."
      }
    },
    {
